<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun west, rain east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun west, rain east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Monday were forecast to see sun in the west, and showers in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see sun and highs of 18 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see clear skies in the west but cloud and showers in the east with highs of 18 to 23 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sun in the south, showers in the central region with highs of 20 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
